<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Untuned placeholder: the protection, insulation, mass and cost are a copy of VFEP's
    VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Siegebreaker (VFEP v3.09, 1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml)
    until the set's own tuning lands; see the armor def's header for the reference tables and
    the art and tint-mask note. Siegebreaker's EnergyShieldRechargeRate offset is not copied: it
    is a thing-level stat, so an offset on a pawn's apparel never reaches the armor's shield.

    The medic offsets are this set's own, and first guesses for the tuning pass. MedicalTendSpeed
    +0.25 is about four Medicine levels on vanilla's skill curve for that stat. The Manipulation
    floor of 1.0 only matters to an impaired pilot (a floor never lowers a capacity) and feeds
    both tend stats through their Manipulation capacity factor. Both reach the mechanite dressing
    through vanilla's tend formula.

    Adrenaline shot: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants MDWC_AdrenalineShot (AbilityDefs/
    AdrenalineShot.xml), fed by the injector beside it, a plain vanilla CompApparelReloadable
    the ability reads off the apparel that grants it, so both comps sit on this one def (the
    Aerial shoulders' pairing). ammoCountPerCharge 1: one item loads one shot. With it set,
    vanilla's NeedsReload is remaining != max on both the idle and the forced path, so
    colonists fetch an item for every empty slot, and ReloadFrom adds min(stack / perCharge,
    max - remaining), so a forced reload never discards anything. Refill mode
    (ammoCountToRefill) is not used: a multi-shot refill item leaves the pilot on its last
    shot until empty or throws the remainder away on an early reload, while a per-item charge
    has no remainder. The per-fight budget is the loaded count, since a drafted pilot cannot
    reload. ammoDef MedicineIndustrial: adrenaline is epinephrine, a cardiac drug drawn from a
    medical kit, which fits the heart-attack rule, and an industrial kit is 18 silver at market
    value. ammoDef and maxCharges 3 are mod settings defaulting to these values; the ammo
    setting also writes the item's uiIcon onto the ability as its placeholder art. The free
    first fill is three industrial kits (54 silver), to be priced into the costList in the
    tuning pass. chargeNoun "shot": the inspect line, the stat sheet and the empty message
    count in shots. No verbs, so the comp draws no gizmo of its own; the ability's command
    shows the count. Its DefInjected keys read comps.CompApparelReloadable, the vanilla comp
    class.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy
    keeps its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml and the VGE vacuum patch leave shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's and
    VGE1's own patches do for VFEP's.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>MDWC_WarcasketShoulders_Medic</defName>
    <label>medic warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, fitted with field-medicine manipulators and an adrenaline injector.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, fitted with field-medicine manipulators and an adrenaline injector.\n\nA 10th-generation spacer chassis refitted for the medic's role: the pilot is welded in for good, like any warcasket wearer, but this one is built to keep the rest of the squad alive rather than to break the line.\n\nThe medic series trades firepower for the tools to treat wounds under fire, so a squad that fields one can stay in the fight long after its stims and bandages have run out.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicShoulders</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <MedicalTendSpeed>0.25</MedicalTendSpeed>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedicShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_ApparelReloadable">
        <maxCharges>3</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>MedicineIndustrial</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>shot</chargeNoun>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>MDWC_AdrenalineShot</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>1.0</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
